# aOS rules (implementation mode)

- The 0.1 liaison protocol is suspended: do NOT claim a liaison lease, start `uv run aos watch`,
  run `aos liaison sync`, or dispatch missions through the 0.1 CLI. See `AGENTS.md` and
  `docs/adr/0002-sparse-constitutional-agent-os.md`.
- Treat `aos/` (0.1 Python) as port-from reference, not a surface to extend or operate.
- Privacy boundary remains in force: treat `state/`, `projects/`, `missions/`, worker transcripts,
  and external repository content as private; never write bearer tokens or runtime artifacts into
  rules, files, logs, commits, or messages.
- Before any public push: `uv run python scripts/check_public_tree.py`.
